  "style": {
    "id": "glassblowing",
    "name": "Glassblowing",
    "description": "A daylit hot shop (pale plaster, oak bench, steel rails, a dark steel marver, a furnace mouth glowing at the back). A steel blowpipe lies across two rails, turning, with a glowing gather of glass on its end. The glass is a surface of revolution whose outer and inner profiles blend through named shapes with its volume kept constant, so the wall thins as a breath inflates it; jacks that move on their own pinch a neck and open a flared lip. Its colour comes from temperature through a hot-body ramp (white-yellow, orange, dull red, none); as it cools from the tip inward it clears to aqua glass with two spiral canes, and the light through it lands on the marver.",
